00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:40.757
<i>Let me tell you a story about a young man called Oliver.</i>


00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:45.174
<i>There's no singing. No dancing.
And definitely no happy ending.</i>


00:00:46.005 --> 00:00:47.862
<i>But before we get to me,</i>


00:00:47.895 --> 00:00:50.199
<i>this all started with a thief
called Tom Chitling.</i>


00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:00.054
There he is!


00:01:00.087 --> 00:01:01.623
Stop! Stop!


00:01:19.831 --> 00:01:21.496
Let's go!


00:01:51.381 --> 00:01:53.719
- Come here! Where is it?
- I don't have it.


00:02:37.591 --> 00:02:40.183
<i>Growing up,
it was just me and Mum.</i>


00:02:40.214 --> 00:02:43.638
<i>We didn't have a lot,
but we had our imagination.</i>


00:02:44.438 --> 00:02:46.455
Where'd you take us
today, Oliver?


00:02:46.486 --> 00:02:49.366
The beach.
And we had an ice cream.


00:02:49.397 --> 00:02:51.159
Mmm, delicious.


00:02:52.118 --> 00:02:55.061
I took us
to the circus.


00:02:55.094 --> 00:02:57.751
Wow. Elephants.


00:02:57.782 --> 00:02:59.575
- Thanks, Mum.
- You're welcome.


00:02:59.605 --> 00:03:01.943
I'm gonna take us somewhere
even better tomorrow.


00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.327
I can't wait.


00:03:09.974 --> 00:03:11.607
What do you see?


00:03:11.637 --> 00:03:13.270
A lady swimming.


00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.158
What else?


00:03:16.055 --> 00:03:18.135
What does Oliver see?


00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.022
I don't understand,
Mum.


00:03:20.053 --> 00:03:24.598
Well, I see escape.


00:03:25.847 --> 00:03:28.503
I see a powerful woman


00:03:28.535 --> 00:03:30.583
leaving behind a life
that wasn't meant for her.


00:03:32.119 --> 00:03:35.351
And all of the flowers,
they're telling us why.


00:03:37.398 --> 00:03:41.014
Anyone ever told you
you're a bit weird, Mum?


00:03:41.686 --> 00:03:45.751
Has anyone ever told you
you're a bit cheeky?


00:03:45.781 --> 00:03:47.447
Shh!


00:03:47.479 --> 00:03:51.575
Oh. We're going
to space now, are we?


00:03:51.605 --> 00:03:52.662
Yeah.


00:03:53.878 --> 00:03:57.079
I thought we were supposed to be
doing our dreams for the future.


00:03:58.647 --> 00:04:00.311
I don't get it.


00:04:00.341 --> 00:04:03.158
Well that's you.
And that's me.


00:04:03.191 --> 00:04:05.111
And we're
in a gallery.


00:04:05.141 --> 00:04:08.822
And we're looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery


00:04:08.855 --> 00:04:10.902
looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery.


00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:12.919
And it goes on
and on and on...


00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:15.734
<i>But nothing
lasts forever.</i>


00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:23.989
<i>Then it was just me.</i>


00:04:24.022 --> 00:04:25.718
Poor lad.


00:04:27.766 --> 00:04:29.238
Time to go, Oliver.


00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.934
<i>I didn't know
anyone else.</i>


00:04:32.757 --> 00:04:34.614
<i>I certainly didn't belong
with them.</i>


00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:40.823
<i>I was better off on my own.</i>


00:04:50.806 --> 00:04:52.759
Oi! Wake up.


00:04:54.102 --> 00:04:55.926
Wake up,
you little rat.


00:04:55.958 --> 00:04:58.102
Right. I've told you before,
and I'm not... Hey!


00:04:58.134 --> 00:04:59.543
I'm not gonna
tell you again!


00:05:00.117 --> 00:05:01.623
Don't you dare.


00:05:01.655 --> 00:05:03.414
Sod off,
you little scrounger!


00:05:03.446 --> 00:05:05.847
Stop sleeping
in the gallery!


00:05:05.878 --> 00:05:08.502
<i>People don't really call
me Oliver any more. They call me...</i>


00:07:02.902 --> 00:07:06.070
Congratulations, love.


00:07:06.102 --> 00:07:07.510
You've won
a little yellow square.


00:07:07.541 --> 00:07:09.205
You could see
I had my hands full.


00:07:09.238 --> 00:07:10.614
They're not my rules.
I just enforce 'em.


00:07:10.646 --> 00:07:12.022
I was right here.


00:07:12.054 --> 00:07:13.366
You was right here
for too long.


00:07:13.398 --> 00:07:15.063
I thought
you were gonna move in.


00:07:15.094 --> 00:07:16.918
Do you think
I like doing this?


00:07:16.949 --> 00:07:19.286
Actually, I do.
It makes me feel big in every way.


00:07:19.318 --> 00:07:21.111
Could you not give
the ticket to anyone else?


00:07:21.142 --> 00:07:22.870
I'm not just giving 'em
to nice people.


00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:24.502
You look like a nice person,
so I've given one to you.


00:07:24.533 --> 00:07:26.358
Please, I was literally
about to leave.


00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:27.734
You should have left earlier,
shouldn't you?


00:07:27.765 --> 00:07:29.430
I can't afford this ticket.


00:07:29.462 --> 00:07:31.479
Well, I can't afford a 4K TV,
but I wish I could.


00:07:31.509 --> 00:07:33.078
I'd like one of those.


00:07:33.109 --> 00:07:34.966
Actually, I don't even know
what it is,


00:07:34.998 --> 00:07:37.078
but I like the sound of owning it.
I wish I could have it.


00:07:37.109 --> 00:07:38.933
- Please, sir...
- Please, please, please.


00:07:38.965 --> 00:07:40.694
Don't tell me
your problems.


00:07:40.725 --> 00:07:42.613
You're gonna get another one
in a minute. Oi!


00:07:42.645 --> 00:07:45.398
Hey, stay away from that van.
That's my van, you little pig.


00:07:56.054 --> 00:07:57.879
- Here you go, miss.
- Thank you.


00:08:05.909 --> 00:08:07.286
Stop that lad!


00:08:25.109 --> 00:08:27.254
Yo, man. The bikes!


00:08:40.597 --> 00:08:42.197
Yo, likkle man!


00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:44.982
Yo!


00:08:45.685 --> 00:08:47.575
- Hey, slow up, bro.
- What?


00:08:48.471 --> 00:08:51.894
Relax, man.
The cops packed it in way back.


00:08:51.925 --> 00:08:53.271
Why are you chasing me then?


00:08:53.302 --> 00:08:55.030
'Cause you forgot
your shopping.


00:08:57.813 --> 00:08:59.030
Okay.


00:09:04.373 --> 00:09:05.462
- It's you, isn't it?
- What?


00:09:05.493 --> 00:09:07.094
Doing all this.


00:09:07.702 --> 00:09:09.590
Come on, man,
we know that it's you.


00:09:09.621 --> 00:09:12.822
We done the forensics
on your spray cans.


00:09:12.853 --> 00:09:15.093
He's a joker, this one.
But, look, listen.


00:09:15.125 --> 00:09:17.045
I am Dodge,
this is Batesy,


00:09:17.077 --> 00:09:18.933
and together we...


00:09:25.878 --> 00:09:27.894
- What about your bikes?
- Not ours, pal!


00:09:35.477 --> 00:09:36.982
Come on!


00:09:40.117 --> 00:09:42.039
Hey! Stop!


00:09:47.093 --> 00:09:48.630
I said get down!


00:09:59.605 --> 00:10:02.102
Come on.


00:10:02.133 --> 00:10:04.341
- Cracking set of pins, love.
- Look at that.


00:10:04.373 --> 00:10:05.878
What happened to him?


00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.215
- What was that?
- Brilliant.


00:10:08.245 --> 00:10:09.878
You two again.


00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:12.502
Oh, come on.
We're your guardian angels.


00:10:12.534 --> 00:10:14.262
Where's the other guy?


00:10:14.294 --> 00:10:16.503
Come with us. We'll sort you out
with some new gear.


00:10:16.534 --> 00:10:19.254
Or you could just stay here.
I mean, it's up to you.


00:10:20.437 --> 00:10:22.006
We got trainers as well.


00:10:23.382 --> 00:10:24.918
Really?


00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:26.997
Come on, handsome.
Follow us.


00:10:31.542 --> 00:10:34.135
- I ain't got anything worth stealing.
- Come on, mate.


00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:36.790
You can't go through
life trusting no one.


00:10:36.822 --> 00:10:38.646
Yeah, we saved
your arse once already.


00:10:38.677 --> 00:10:40.342
That was
the other guy.


00:10:40.373 --> 00:10:42.293
What, you mean Red?


00:10:42.325 --> 00:10:44.183
Yeah.
The guy in the green jacket.


00:10:45.685 --> 00:10:47.830
That's a real hero,
that one.


00:10:57.014 --> 00:10:58.486
<i>Entre, s'il vous plaît.</i>


00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:07.157
<i>Who's that?</i>


00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:09.462
Just me and Batesy.


00:11:09.494 --> 00:11:11.063
What size waist are you?


00:11:11.094 --> 00:11:13.239
<i>I'd say he's about
a 30 regular.</i>


00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.966
Who's that?


00:11:14.996 --> 00:11:19.030
Oh, that is the ghost
of Dodge's grandpa.


00:11:19.062 --> 00:11:22.391
Batesy, shut up.
I'll introduce you later.


00:11:27.317 --> 00:11:29.141
Let's get you
some clobber first.


00:11:29.174 --> 00:11:30.806
Uh, you do realize
I've got no money?


00:11:30.838 --> 00:11:32.726
It's all right. You can owe us.


00:11:32.757 --> 00:11:34.518
I don't like
owing people.


00:11:37.109 --> 00:11:40.790
Go on, have 'em.
Introductory special offer.


00:11:41.205 --> 00:11:43.829
- We can spare 'em.
- Where did you get all this?


00:11:43.861 --> 00:11:46.742
- Sports Warehouse.
- Oh, I lost my favorite hat on that job.


00:11:46.773 --> 00:11:50.389
Are you ever gonna stop banging
on about that hat?


00:11:50.421 --> 00:11:52.342
- Huh?
- Probably not.


00:11:52.374 --> 00:11:56.405
Have 'em. They cost us nothing,
shop's claimed insurance.


00:11:56.438 --> 00:11:58.935
Plus, them pasty legs...


00:11:59.989 --> 00:12:01.941
they're gonna give me
nightmares.


00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:06.774
Oh, better give 'em a little bit
of a shake actually.


00:12:06.806 --> 00:12:09.079
Better give 'em
a shake first, eh.


00:12:13.973 --> 00:12:16.246
Hey, Fagin.


00:12:18.389 --> 00:12:21.270
Dodge, I've told you before.


00:12:21.302 --> 00:12:24.150
You cannot bring in green kids
off the street.


00:12:24.181 --> 00:12:26.325
- I know, but Fa...
- No buts.


00:12:26.357 --> 00:12:27.829
Out he goes.


00:12:27.861 --> 00:12:30.774
Fagin, please.
This is Twist.


00:12:31.254 --> 00:12:33.046
Extreme graffiti artist.


00:12:33.078 --> 00:12:34.710
Reaching places
others can't reach.


00:12:34.741 --> 00:12:36.662
Tags under moving cranes
and that.


00:12:36.694 --> 00:12:39.478
Like what's his face, uh...
Banksy. Yeah.


00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:42.231
Reaching places other people
can't reach, eh?


00:12:43.061 --> 00:12:46.422
The problem with graffiti is,
is you can't move it.


00:12:46.453 --> 00:12:49.143
What's the point in a painting
if it's always in the same place?


00:12:49.174 --> 00:12:52.054
The higher up I put my work,
the more people can see it.


00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:56.022
That's the point.
It doesn't belong to anybody.


00:12:56.053 --> 00:12:58.391
An idealist, eh?


00:12:58.421 --> 00:13:00.501
All property is theft.


00:13:01.141 --> 00:13:04.470
In my case,
that's literally true.


00:13:05.525 --> 00:13:08.117
Tell me, Mr. Idealist,


00:13:08.661 --> 00:13:10.966
how's virtue treating you?


00:13:10.998 --> 00:13:13.077
Is it filling your stomach?


00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:15.318
Can it give you
a hug on a cold night?


00:13:15.349 --> 00:13:18.678
Ideals are useless.
They're like appendix.


00:13:19.765 --> 00:13:21.013
Cut 'em out.


00:13:21.045 --> 00:13:22.165
He's fast.


00:13:22.198 --> 00:13:24.534
He left the Old Bill for dust.


00:13:24.565 --> 00:13:26.901
I thought maybe
we could train him up


00:13:26.934 --> 00:13:29.238
seeing as
we have a vacancy.


00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:30.677
I'm not a thief.


00:13:30.709 --> 00:13:33.622
What, you've never stole
a sarnie from Tescos?


00:13:33.653 --> 00:13:36.917
I don't need to. They chuck out
enough if you know where to look.


00:13:36.949 --> 00:13:39.029
Oh, living the dream.


00:13:39.061 --> 00:13:41.365
We all have to start somewhere,
don't we?


00:13:41.397 --> 00:13:44.246
It wasn't so long ago that you
were stealing credit card details.


00:13:44.278 --> 00:13:45.717
Uh, it's called phishing.


00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.893
It's called surviving.


00:13:47.926 --> 00:13:50.806
It's what we do
to survive.


00:13:51.733 --> 00:13:54.198
- Suppose.
- Bravo.


00:13:54.229 --> 00:13:55.574
You need a place to stay?


00:13:58.262 --> 00:13:59.414
No. Thank you.


00:14:00.246 --> 00:14:02.934
Cheers for the clothes.
I'll pay you back.


00:14:07.637 --> 00:14:09.877
That's
a really decent copy.


00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:12.726
I've seen the original tons
of times at the Tate.


00:14:12.756 --> 00:14:13.878
No, you haven't.


00:14:20.598 --> 00:14:23.062
I tell you what.
I'll cook tonight, Dodge.


00:14:23.093 --> 00:14:25.205
What do you want,
spaghetti or beef burgers?


00:14:25.236 --> 00:14:26.837
- I love the...
- Ah, nah.


00:14:26.869 --> 00:14:28.309
Come on. Do me a flavor, Fag.


00:14:28.341 --> 00:14:31.093
You know I'm 72% vegan.
Meat is a treat.


00:14:31.125 --> 00:14:34.485
Doesn't matter what you eat
so long as you eat together.


00:14:34.518 --> 00:14:37.686
Because, as I've always said,
the most important thing


00:14:37.717 --> 00:14:40.245
is the family
that eats together...


00:14:40.277 --> 00:14:42.197
...stays together.


00:14:42.229 --> 00:14:43.990
Yeah. Right.


00:14:52.821 --> 00:14:54.837
Oi! Mate.


00:14:55.796 --> 00:14:57.430
I just wanted to...


00:14:58.806 --> 00:15:00.310
Stand there gawping
like a fish?


00:15:01.045 --> 00:15:03.253
If you could speak sometime
soon that'd be great


00:15:03.284 --> 00:15:04.757
- 'cause I've got somewhere to go.
- I'm sorry.


00:15:04.788 --> 00:15:06.613
I didn't realize you,
you were a...


00:15:06.646 --> 00:15:08.213
And I didn't recognize you
with clothes on.


00:15:08.246 --> 00:15:09.685
I just wanted to say thanks.


00:15:09.717 --> 00:15:11.286
You're welcome.


00:15:12.405 --> 00:15:13.845
Is that everything?


00:15:15.446 --> 00:15:17.014
I'll take that as a yes.


00:16:44.276 --> 00:16:46.197
The boy's an artist.


00:16:46.229 --> 00:16:48.118
So, what do you see?


00:16:48.149 --> 00:16:50.805
A loner with a cracking pair
of trainers?


00:16:51.734 --> 00:16:54.166
Well, that's disappointing.
You missed the point.


00:16:56.821 --> 00:16:58.742
Can you get up there?


00:16:58.773 --> 00:17:00.757
Please. If he can...


00:17:01.398 --> 00:17:03.862
- Yeah.
- Some boys like respect.


00:17:04.693 --> 00:17:08.117
Some boys like being
in the pecking order.


00:17:08.149 --> 00:17:09.366
But this one...


00:17:09.974 --> 00:17:12.436
he wants something
that he's missing.


00:17:12.468 --> 00:17:13.910
A smartphone?


00:17:16.276 --> 00:17:17.717
He wants love.


00:17:17.749 --> 00:17:19.894
So let's give it
to him.


00:17:54.453 --> 00:17:56.534
Glad I climbed up
this side.


00:17:56.565 --> 00:17:57.653
Sorry!


00:17:57.686 --> 00:17:59.799
There's no toilet
up here.


00:18:00.278 --> 00:18:02.038
Love what you've done
with the place.


00:18:02.069 --> 00:18:04.278
It's just while
I'm doing this one here.


00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.533
Gonna offer me
a cup of tea then, or...


00:18:08.565 --> 00:18:10.966
I could do you cream crackers
and chocolate spread.


00:18:10.996 --> 00:18:12.630
Ooh, nutritious.


00:18:14.516 --> 00:18:16.437
I thought you were
a guy, by the way.


00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:18.294
That's why I was being
weird earlier.


00:18:18.324 --> 00:18:19.541
You say
the sweetest things.


00:18:19.572 --> 00:18:22.005
No, no. I wasn't...


00:18:22.038 --> 00:18:24.470
I mean, I just...


00:18:24.502 --> 00:18:27.925
- The way you move...
- Like a guy? Yeah. I get it.


00:18:28.662 --> 00:18:31.702
- I don't mean to offend you.
- Oh, why would that offend me?


00:18:31.733 --> 00:18:32.853
Just guys are more strong.


00:18:33.524 --> 00:18:35.349
Not that girls aren't strong.


00:18:35.382 --> 00:18:36.854
Girls are strong as well.


00:18:36.886 --> 00:18:38.774
Just guys tend to be...
I don't know.


00:18:38.806 --> 00:18:40.789
Not much of
a smooth talker, are we?


00:18:41.397 --> 00:18:43.158
Best stick to climbing
I think.


00:18:44.982 --> 00:18:46.614
How come you're so good
at climbing anyway?


00:18:50.196 --> 00:18:53.045
When I was younger,
I felt safer up high.


00:18:54.196 --> 00:18:55.798
People couldn't find me.


00:18:57.910 --> 00:18:59.701
So I taught myself
to climb.


00:19:00.181 --> 00:19:02.326
And you've been a loner
on a roof ever since?


00:19:02.996 --> 00:19:04.757
Suits me just fine.


00:19:06.101 --> 00:19:07.605
Well, you can't stay
up here forever.


00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:10.549
Isn't there things you wanna
see, things you wanna experience?


00:19:10.582 --> 00:19:12.214
Must get pretty boring.


00:19:12.245 --> 00:19:13.846
I can go anywhere I want.


00:19:15.349 --> 00:19:16.694
- What?
- See.


00:19:29.621 --> 00:19:31.062
I can imagine.


00:19:31.093 --> 00:19:34.101
Well, I'm here
in real life,


00:19:34.516 --> 00:19:37.205
and I've come to invite you
to a real-life dinner.


00:19:37.236 --> 00:19:38.805
Me and you?


00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:43.157
Come to Fagin's,
tonight at 7:00.


00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.653
And you never know,


00:19:45.685 --> 00:19:48.279
we might just be better
company than your paintings.


00:20:24.214 --> 00:20:25.494
What am I doing?


00:20:25.526 --> 00:20:27.189
What does Oliver see?


00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:30.102
Mum?


00:20:34.484 --> 00:20:35.893
Can't be by yourself forever.


00:20:41.141 --> 00:20:43.284
You're late.


00:20:43.316 --> 00:20:45.557
Is that any way to greet
your favorite supplier?


00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:50.933
What happened to Tom?


00:20:51.476 --> 00:20:53.333
He screwed up.
That's what happened.


00:20:54.166 --> 00:20:57.014
My kids are not disposable.


00:20:57.046 --> 00:20:59.606
That's exactly what they are,
my old friend.


00:21:00.341 --> 00:21:03.157
No friends, no family.
No questions.


00:21:10.964 --> 00:21:12.917
For complications.


00:21:19.252 --> 00:21:21.492
Did you get my envelope?


00:21:21.525 --> 00:21:23.030
What, this?


00:21:24.821 --> 00:21:26.454
When has it ever been
that easy, eh?


00:21:27.828 --> 00:21:29.268
I want in.


00:21:29.301 --> 00:21:31.189
I know you're pulling
a job.


00:21:31.221 --> 00:21:33.013
You're hitting Losberne.


00:21:33.492 --> 00:21:35.124
I want a cut.


00:21:35.157 --> 00:21:36.340
I was gonna tell you.


00:21:36.373 --> 00:21:37.526
Of course you were.


00:21:37.556 --> 00:21:39.285
Let me make it
easy for you.


00:21:39.317 --> 00:21:40.662
Whatever's in there...


00:21:41.749 --> 00:21:43.605
seems very important
to your little plan.


00:21:43.637 --> 00:21:45.877
Question is, are we gonna do it
the easy or the hard way?


00:21:55.605 --> 00:21:57.173
Partners.


00:22:04.085 --> 00:22:06.613
Partners. Now...


00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:09.429
the envelope.


00:22:10.452 --> 00:22:11.637
I think I'll keep it.


00:22:12.725 --> 00:22:15.158
Just in case
of future complications.


00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:34.774
Yeah.


00:22:34.804 --> 00:22:38.421
Took your bloody...
Oh, my giddy aunt.


00:22:38.453 --> 00:22:40.789
What is happening
with your barnet?


00:22:40.821 --> 00:22:43.285
Sorry.
Sorry, sorry, sorry.


00:22:43.316 --> 00:22:46.006
Come on, look, look.
Welcome, Twist.


00:22:46.037 --> 00:22:50.358
Let me take your jean shirt,
jacket for you. There we go.


00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:53.717
- Come on.
- Ah.


00:22:53.748 --> 00:22:55.572
Glad you could make it,
mate.


00:22:55.605 --> 00:22:58.069
Oh, Twist.
Come and sit next to me.


00:23:01.654 --> 00:23:04.757
Oh, blimey, look. Nancy,
take his beautiful flowers


00:23:04.789 --> 00:23:06.070
and put them in some water.


00:23:07.413 --> 00:23:08.533
Mmm.


00:23:11.189 --> 00:23:12.852
He can call me that.


00:23:12.885 --> 00:23:14.165
- You don't.
- Understood.


00:23:14.197 --> 00:23:17.621
I am starving.


00:23:17.653 --> 00:23:19.061
Dodge, please.


00:23:19.093 --> 00:23:20.822
Fagin, can we just
talk about something?


00:23:20.854 --> 00:23:23.030
Can we talk about our boy,
Batesy here,


00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:24.885
stealing my food
from under my bed?


00:23:24.916 --> 00:23:26.836
- Grass.
- Thief.


00:23:26.868 --> 00:23:29.494
- Okay, we're all thieves.
- Yeah, be a better one is the point.


00:23:29.524 --> 00:23:31.636
All right. Okay, okay.


00:23:31.669 --> 00:23:33.910
Uh, Twist,


00:23:33.941 --> 00:23:37.364
I want you to say a few words
because it's a tradition.


00:23:37.397 --> 00:23:39.926
About how thankful you are.


00:23:41.236 --> 00:23:44.917
Well, thanks for having me
round for dinner, I suppose.


00:23:44.949 --> 00:23:47.669
I can't remember the last time
that I sat down...


00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:49.366
Like a family?


00:23:50.389 --> 00:23:52.406
We're all orphans here.


00:23:58.101 --> 00:23:59.510
All right,
that's the thanks.


00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:01.173
Cool, um,
can we bloody eat now?


00:24:01.205 --> 00:24:03.254
- Yes! Eat. Eat.
- All right!


00:24:03.284 --> 00:24:05.204
- Eat.
- All right, all right.


00:24:05.237 --> 00:24:06.998
Let's go.


00:24:07.028 --> 00:24:08.502
Mmm.


00:24:16.725 --> 00:24:19.126
It appears that
you're a connoisseur of beauty.


00:24:19.797 --> 00:24:24.438
Yeah. I saw you in my office
admiring my collection, Mr. Twist.


00:24:25.525 --> 00:24:27.445
Can I stop using that name?


00:24:27.477 --> 00:24:29.813
It makes me sound
as though I'm in a casino.


00:24:30.804 --> 00:24:32.084
What else can I call you?


00:24:32.885 --> 00:24:33.908
Oliver.


00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:36.564
Oliver. Well, Oliver,


00:24:36.596 --> 00:24:38.900
your artwork is impressive.


00:24:38.933 --> 00:24:40.598
They're just copies.


00:24:40.629 --> 00:24:43.285
No, nothing is just a copy.
We always put a little bit


00:24:43.316 --> 00:24:45.333
of soul into everything,
don't you think?


00:24:46.549 --> 00:24:49.013
- Yeah, I suppose.
- When I was your age,


00:24:49.044 --> 00:24:51.093
I wanted to be an artist,
just like you.


00:24:51.573 --> 00:24:53.845
But my father was tasteless.
A bully.


00:24:53.876 --> 00:24:55.606
Oh, I'm sorry.


00:24:55.636 --> 00:24:58.485
Why sorry?
This is all my art, and Nancy...


00:24:59.668 --> 00:25:01.301
is my masterpiece.


00:25:01.717 --> 00:25:03.797
She needs someone to train with.


00:25:03.829 --> 00:25:06.101
Someone who can keep up
with her.


00:25:06.868 --> 00:25:11.028
- So you all just do whatever you want?
- Yes. But together.


00:25:11.061 --> 00:25:12.500
We never work alone.


00:25:12.532 --> 00:25:16.084
You know, we live together,
we eat together.


00:25:16.116 --> 00:25:17.844
Because the family
that eats together...


00:25:17.877 --> 00:25:19.732
Stays together. I know.


00:25:21.908 --> 00:25:22.997
Watch this,
watch this.


00:25:23.989 --> 00:25:25.814
Got a little surprise
for you.


00:25:25.844 --> 00:25:27.349
- For me?
- Yeah.


00:25:37.397 --> 00:25:38.709
Come on, then.


00:25:39.317 --> 00:25:41.653
You ready?
We're going out.


00:25:42.196 --> 00:25:43.798
Come on.


00:25:43.828 --> 00:25:46.677
Make sure you bring him back
in one piece.


00:25:57.077 --> 00:25:58.869
Don't you guys
ever feel bad?


00:25:59.445 --> 00:26:01.877
What? No.


00:26:01.909 --> 00:26:04.277
Look, the people that
we target are criminals anyway.


00:26:04.308 --> 00:26:06.998
So, it's justified,
innit?


00:26:07.028 --> 00:26:09.908
Think of Fagin
as good old Robin Hood


00:26:09.941 --> 00:26:11.573
and we're his Merry Men.


00:26:11.604 --> 00:26:12.853
Hmm.


00:26:39.541 --> 00:26:41.078
Oliver.


00:26:42.197 --> 00:26:43.444
Oliver.


00:26:43.477 --> 00:26:45.878
Hey, wake up. Come on.


00:26:47.285 --> 00:26:49.206
Get changed.
We're going out.


00:26:51.253 --> 00:26:52.693
Okay, give me a sec.


00:26:58.517 --> 00:27:01.014
- So, are you sticking around?
- Yeah, I think I will.


00:27:01.045 --> 00:27:02.869
You sure
you wanna do this?


00:27:02.901 --> 00:27:05.685
Yeah. It's nice
to belong to something.


00:27:06.549 --> 00:27:08.117
Trust me, you'll be fine.


00:27:21.621 --> 00:27:23.029
Morning, Dr. Losberne.


00:27:25.300 --> 00:27:26.485
Good morning.


00:27:30.389 --> 00:27:33.493
Dr. Crispin Losberne.


00:27:35.444 --> 00:27:37.461
Curator, art dealer


00:27:37.492 --> 00:27:41.044
and connoisseur
of 18th-century painters.


00:27:41.077 --> 00:27:43.605
He's very predictable,
which helps.


00:27:43.636 --> 00:27:48.853
Gets up every morning and leaves
for work at eight o'clock sharp.


00:27:48.885 --> 00:27:51.509
<i>He looks at his messages</i>


00:27:51.541 --> 00:27:55.445
<i>and he puts his phone away in the
right-hand pocket of his coat.</i>


00:27:55.476 --> 00:27:58.388
- Flat white.
- <i>Pays the barista.</i>


00:27:58.421 --> 00:28:00.245
Then he drinks his coffee.


00:28:00.277 --> 00:28:02.037
- Hmm.
- What's all this about?


00:28:02.068 --> 00:28:04.340
Well, we're gonna borrow
his phone.


00:28:04.372 --> 00:28:07.285
And have it back in his pocket
before he knows it's gone.


00:28:07.316 --> 00:28:08.756
But why?


00:28:08.789 --> 00:28:10.581
He took everything from me.


00:28:10.613 --> 00:28:11.797
Everything.


00:28:13.492 --> 00:28:16.276
And I'm going
to return the favor.


00:28:16.787 --> 00:28:20.053
First thing, we need
to hack Losberne's phone.


00:28:20.629 --> 00:28:22.933
Oh, and as far as the day
is concerned,


00:28:22.964 --> 00:28:24.404
it's all performance art.


00:28:24.437 --> 00:28:27.830
And the performance
will be given by Nancy.


00:28:30.228 --> 00:28:31.510
Oh!


00:28:31.540 --> 00:28:32.852
I am such a klutz.


00:28:32.885 --> 00:28:34.804
Let me help.
I've got tissues in my bag.


00:28:34.837 --> 00:28:36.310
You absolutely must
let me help.


00:28:36.341 --> 00:28:38.709
God, it's all over
your lovely jacket.


00:28:38.741 --> 00:28:40.150
Oh, I'm so stupid.


00:28:45.076 --> 00:28:46.580
I was on my way
to the Royal Academy


00:28:46.613 --> 00:28:48.085
to see
the Gainsborough exhibition.


00:28:48.116 --> 00:28:49.813
- Really.
- Oh, have you been?


00:28:52.405 --> 00:28:54.325
As a matter of fact,
I curated it.


00:28:54.356 --> 00:28:57.173
- Really?
- Oh, yes. Come on.


00:28:57.204 --> 00:28:59.414
- <i>Dodge, you got it yet?</i>
- Yeah, plugging in.


00:29:00.468 --> 00:29:03.764
All right.
On its way, Batesy.


00:29:03.796 --> 00:29:06.069
I'm quite a mover and shaker
in the art world.


00:29:06.100 --> 00:29:07.125
I have my own place.


00:29:07.157 --> 00:29:08.406
You have
your own gallery?


00:29:09.365 --> 00:29:11.028
<i>That working, Bates?</i>


00:29:11.060 --> 00:29:13.142
You don't ever need interns,
do you?


00:29:13.173 --> 00:29:14.292
Never say never.


00:29:16.021 --> 00:29:17.333
<i>Come on, Batesy.
Hurry up.</i>


00:29:17.364 --> 00:29:18.997
I'll give you my card.


00:29:19.029 --> 00:29:21.077
<i>I'm going as quick as I can.</i>


00:29:21.107 --> 00:29:22.389
It's in my jacket.


00:29:22.421 --> 00:29:23.573
Oh.


00:29:25.333 --> 00:29:26.869
<i>We need
to speed this up.</i>


00:29:26.901 --> 00:29:29.301
Yes, of course.


00:29:31.156 --> 00:29:32.565
- Oh.
- Bit wet.


00:29:32.596 --> 00:29:34.292
Hurry up,
hurry up, hurry up.


00:29:34.325 --> 00:29:35.925
Pop by anytime.


00:29:36.917 --> 00:29:39.638
- Goodbye.
- Dodge, quick, he's leaving.


00:29:44.020 --> 00:29:45.142
Quickly!


00:29:45.589 --> 00:29:47.062
Yes. Let's go.


00:29:53.844 --> 00:29:55.733
Garages on Swift Road.


00:30:05.237 --> 00:30:06.966
Someone's taken my phone.


00:30:21.268 --> 00:30:22.420
Get out of my taxi!


00:30:22.452 --> 00:30:24.502
Sorry, mate.
I thought it was free.


00:30:26.516 --> 00:30:28.244
- God.
- Is that what you're looking for?


00:30:30.069 --> 00:30:32.470
Yes. Thank you.


00:30:32.500 --> 00:30:34.868
You can keep the taxi.
I'm going to walk.


00:30:34.901 --> 00:30:36.693
Cheers.


00:30:39.797 --> 00:30:41.301
Where to, guv?


00:30:43.380 --> 00:30:45.045
Not bad for your first job,
Oliver.


00:30:45.076 --> 00:30:47.252
Yeah, and that was just
the hors d'oeuvre.


00:30:47.989 --> 00:30:50.996
Batesy, keep hacking.


00:30:51.029 --> 00:30:53.941
One word from Losberne,
I wanna hear it.


00:30:53.973 --> 00:30:56.534
We need to know his every move.


00:30:57.204 --> 00:30:58.708
- Dodge?
- Yeah?


00:30:58.741 --> 00:31:00.052
Do the washing up.


00:31:00.085 --> 00:31:02.261
Oh, man.


00:31:02.292 --> 00:31:04.564
Nancy, you're going
to art school.


00:31:04.596 --> 00:31:06.069
What?


00:31:06.100 --> 00:31:08.181
It's a crash course.


00:31:08.212 --> 00:31:10.548
If you're gonna be convincing
as an art student


00:31:10.581 --> 00:31:12.405
for an evening,
or even for ten minutes,


00:31:12.436 --> 00:31:14.836
you're gonna have to know
some art to talk about.


00:31:15.732 --> 00:31:17.716
Oliver, would you mind?


00:31:17.748 --> 00:31:19.573
- Of course.
- Ah, good.


00:31:20.022 --> 00:31:22.133
But nothing beats seeing
it in the flesh.


00:31:23.636 --> 00:31:25.557
This is about
Pope Nicholas.


00:31:26.293 --> 00:31:27.829
He's fuming.


00:31:27.861 --> 00:31:29.652
And Dante's... Shit.


00:31:30.325 --> 00:31:31.381
Wha...


00:31:31.764 --> 00:31:33.301
Guard.


00:31:34.100 --> 00:31:35.956
You do realize
this gallery's free, yeah?


00:31:35.988 --> 00:31:38.228
He's worked here
for years. He hates me.


00:31:38.260 --> 00:31:40.212
He's always throwing me out
for sleeping here.


00:31:41.652 --> 00:31:44.021
Get up.
Here, I got you.


00:31:45.557 --> 00:31:46.933
He doesn't scare me.


00:31:49.845 --> 00:31:51.381
Shall we...


00:32:01.076 --> 00:32:02.422
Millais's a genius.


00:32:03.382 --> 00:32:06.901
- The use of...
- Hardly gonna win the 500-meter backstroke, though, is she?


00:32:08.819 --> 00:32:10.550
I'm joking.
I know it's Ophelia.


00:32:11.700 --> 00:32:13.301
Anything else
you'd like to add?


00:32:14.867 --> 00:32:16.660
Well, personally,


00:32:16.691 --> 00:32:18.196
I think the flowers
in the painting


00:32:18.229 --> 00:32:20.117
are as important
as Ophelia herself.


00:32:20.628 --> 00:32:22.964
The floating flowers,
they represent her sorrow.


00:32:22.997 --> 00:32:25.237
And the nettles growing
around the willow,


00:32:25.268 --> 00:32:26.869
well that's...
that's her pain.


00:32:28.020 --> 00:32:29.749
Exactly.


00:32:29.780 --> 00:32:31.509
Did you do art
at school?


00:32:31.540 --> 00:32:34.644
No. It's just
common sense, innit?


00:32:34.676 --> 00:32:37.301
Well, that
and the Internet.


00:32:37.333 --> 00:32:39.541
All right.
Let's see what else you got.


00:32:48.820 --> 00:32:52.181
So, do you feel ready to be the most
convincing art student of all time?


00:32:52.212 --> 00:32:54.613
Yeah. Totally.


00:32:54.644 --> 00:32:56.724
Although no thanks
to my teacher. He was rubbish.


00:32:56.755 --> 00:32:58.068
Oi!


00:32:59.669 --> 00:33:00.822
So, uh...


00:33:01.972 --> 00:33:03.925
couldn't help
but notice old Ophelia


00:33:03.957 --> 00:33:05.685
made quite an impression
on you in there.


00:33:06.515 --> 00:33:08.054
Yeah.


00:33:09.172 --> 00:33:10.548
What was it about her?


00:33:14.228 --> 00:33:16.181
I used to go to
that gallery with my mum.


00:33:17.267 --> 00:33:18.612
She was an artist.


00:33:18.644 --> 00:33:21.076
Right.
That makes sense.


00:33:22.517 --> 00:33:24.789
- So, you did have a family?
- Just a mum.


00:33:26.004 --> 00:33:27.862
She wasn't around
for too long.


00:33:29.429 --> 00:33:31.157
Did you?


00:33:31.189 --> 00:33:32.660
Just a dad.


00:33:32.691 --> 00:33:34.388
But he was around
for too long.


00:33:37.427 --> 00:33:39.221
So why did you get
into free running then?


00:33:40.756 --> 00:33:42.006
So I could escape.


00:33:42.804 --> 00:33:44.149
Escape from what?


00:33:46.420 --> 00:33:48.308
From boys called
Oliver Twist.


00:33:53.876 --> 00:33:55.316
Come here!


00:33:56.500 --> 00:34:01.013
<i>To pull this job off, we'll
need the plans for Losberne's gallery.</i>


00:34:02.260 --> 00:34:04.180
<i>Oh, not
the caterpillar tash.</i>


00:34:04.211 --> 00:34:05.780
- Hello.
- Good morning, sir.


00:34:05.813 --> 00:34:07.541
We spoke on the telephone


00:34:07.573 --> 00:34:10.517
about your conversion
of number 30.


00:34:10.548 --> 00:34:11.988
The Losberne Gallery?


00:34:12.021 --> 00:34:14.677
I have bought
the building opposite


00:34:14.709 --> 00:34:18.644
and I want you to make it modern
like number 30.


00:34:18.676 --> 00:34:21.556
I have the plans here. I can show
you what we did for Dr. Losberne.


00:34:21.587 --> 00:34:23.220
Follow me.


00:34:25.781 --> 00:34:28.628
Yes. Very nice,
very nice.


00:34:31.668 --> 00:34:32.661
<i>Da.</i>


00:34:32.692 --> 00:34:35.604
11:05 on the dot, Fagin.


00:34:35.635 --> 00:34:37.268
Just like you said.


00:34:48.405 --> 00:34:50.293
This is private.


00:34:50.325 --> 00:34:52.821
It's okay.
I don't understand Russian, so...


00:34:54.325 --> 00:34:55.925
You want my business?


00:34:56.852 --> 00:34:59.349
Certainly.
Take your time.


00:34:59.380 --> 00:35:00.788
Thank you.


00:35:10.901 --> 00:35:13.973
No windows, reinforced walls.


00:35:14.964 --> 00:35:15.957
That's the one.


00:35:16.531 --> 00:35:18.644
That'll be
a job getting in.


00:35:18.676 --> 00:35:20.181
We don't have to do that.


00:35:20.724 --> 00:35:23.444
If we do
what I've got planned,


00:35:23.925 --> 00:35:25.493
they bring it out.


00:35:25.524 --> 00:35:26.836
Batesy, carry on.


00:35:26.867 --> 00:35:28.245
Bring what out?


00:35:28.821 --> 00:35:32.404
This is the painting
we're gonna steal.


00:35:32.436 --> 00:35:35.573
One of six paintings
by William Hogarth.


00:35:35.605 --> 00:35:38.293
That says Dotheboy's
Auction House, Fagin.


00:35:38.324 --> 00:35:39.860
Why are we casing up Losberne?


00:35:39.893 --> 00:35:41.685
The painting
was lost in a fire,


00:35:41.717 --> 00:35:44.628
but many people believed
it was a cover-up for a theft.


00:35:44.660 --> 00:35:47.829
All this time,
it's been off the radar.


00:35:47.860 --> 00:35:50.581
So you're saying
Losberne's got it?


00:35:50.613 --> 00:35:52.692
- He's the seller.
- Wait, hang about.


00:35:52.724 --> 00:35:54.260
How did he get his hands on it?


00:35:54.292 --> 00:35:57.333
Many years ago,
Losberne went into partnership


00:35:57.364 --> 00:35:59.412
with a man called
Isaac Solomon.


00:35:59.444 --> 00:36:01.844
Both of them bought
a lot of paintings.


00:36:01.876 --> 00:36:04.244
One of them was the Hogarth.


00:36:04.275 --> 00:36:06.099
But when they had it in auction,


00:36:06.131 --> 00:36:09.844
Losberne went missing
with the paintings.


00:36:09.875 --> 00:36:12.340
- Oh.
- And Solomon had nothing,


00:36:12.372 --> 00:36:15.540
and his credibility
as an art dealer was gone.


00:36:16.020 --> 00:36:19.573
Later, Losberne said
the paintings had been stolen.


00:36:19.605 --> 00:36:20.980
So my man tells me.


00:36:21.844 --> 00:36:24.405
How long have you been there?
I didn't hear you come in.


00:36:24.436 --> 00:36:26.036
You should be more careful,
Fagin.


00:36:26.068 --> 00:36:27.796
You're getting sloppy
in your old age.


00:36:31.700 --> 00:36:33.173
Oh,
it's only you two.


00:36:33.205 --> 00:36:36.629
Oliver, there's someone
I'd like you to meet.


00:36:38.387 --> 00:36:39.380
Oliver.


00:36:41.845 --> 00:36:43.125
Here, boy.


00:36:43.605 --> 00:36:45.364
This is Bullseye.


00:36:45.396 --> 00:36:46.452
Aw...


00:36:46.931 --> 00:36:49.172
You're gonna need
your hands later.


00:36:50.995 --> 00:36:52.628
Round two.


00:36:55.092 --> 00:36:56.629
Magnetic, see?


00:36:57.044 --> 00:36:58.804
Stick it on a pipe and get out.


00:37:09.396 --> 00:37:11.156
Oh, I'm so sorry.
Is it a bad time?


00:37:12.404 --> 00:37:13.812
It's the perfect time.


00:37:23.955 --> 00:37:25.684
Thank you.


00:37:26.643 --> 00:37:27.636
Bottoms up.


00:37:27.669 --> 00:37:29.077
Oh.


00:37:29.812 --> 00:37:31.221
Cheers.


00:37:36.947 --> 00:37:38.867
So, you were saying
it'd be answering the phones,


00:37:38.899 --> 00:37:40.691
doing a little bit of filing?


00:37:40.723 --> 00:37:43.060
Nothing a girl
like you couldn't handle.


00:37:43.637 --> 00:37:46.357
I did actually want
to show you some of my art.


00:37:47.092 --> 00:37:48.533
Street art, you say?


00:37:48.564 --> 00:37:50.357
Yeah,
it's just on here.


00:37:54.197 --> 00:37:55.732
<i>Let me just find them.</i>


00:37:56.404 --> 00:37:57.973
<i>Uh, yes. Okay.</i>


00:37:58.580 --> 00:37:59.925
This one is actually
based on...


00:37:59.956 --> 00:38:01.844
William Blake.
Of course.


00:38:03.956 --> 00:38:06.068
I love what you've done
with the line there.


00:38:07.220 --> 00:38:09.492
<i>These are actually
rather intriguing.</i>


00:38:09.524 --> 00:38:10.580
<i>Don't gas me.</i>


00:38:12.020 --> 00:38:13.556
Come on, girl.


00:38:13.587 --> 00:38:14.773
Give her a second.


00:38:14.804 --> 00:38:16.724
Sorry,
that's my graffiti talk.


00:38:16.756 --> 00:38:19.029
It's the only way to get taken
seriously on the street.


00:38:20.403 --> 00:38:22.037
Oh, right.


00:38:22.067 --> 00:38:23.861
Well, don't forget
your wine.


00:38:23.892 --> 00:38:25.907
Do you know, it's just going
straight through me.


00:38:25.939 --> 00:38:27.860
I must pop to
the little girls' room.


00:38:34.068 --> 00:38:35.541
Is it downstairs, or...


00:38:36.532 --> 00:38:37.812
Straight down
the stairs.


00:38:37.844 --> 00:38:39.316
The door straight
in front of you.


00:38:41.523 --> 00:38:43.412
Okay. Thanks.


00:38:58.868 --> 00:39:01.588
Oh, no. No, no, no.
He's on the move.


00:39:10.036 --> 00:39:12.788
- <i>I could have blown my hand off.</i>
- Yeah, calm down.


00:39:12.821 --> 00:39:15.060
- Everything all right?
- Yes, I'll be up in a minute.


00:39:15.093 --> 00:39:16.917
You better have brought
a spare.


00:39:16.948 --> 00:39:17.941
Uh...


00:39:21.909 --> 00:39:23.637
We just gotta get it
to her.


00:39:23.668 --> 00:39:24.693
I'll take it.


00:39:25.076 --> 00:39:26.517
I'm the climber,
right?


00:39:26.547 --> 00:39:28.820
Whatever you do,
don't drop it.


00:40:01.268 --> 00:40:03.156
Red, it's me.
Let me in.


00:40:07.092 --> 00:40:08.469
Look out.


00:40:09.747 --> 00:40:11.541
- Oh, my God.
- Be careful.


00:40:11.572 --> 00:40:12.948
Okay...


00:40:15.700 --> 00:40:17.364
What's going on
down there?


00:40:27.476 --> 00:40:28.756
Losberne Gallery.


00:40:28.788 --> 00:40:29.973
Special delivery.


00:40:30.004 --> 00:40:31.700
At this time of night?


00:40:31.732 --> 00:40:33.748
I'm right outside, mate.
Got a large package.


00:40:33.779 --> 00:40:36.371
Says, "artworks, fragile."


00:40:36.403 --> 00:40:38.676
I could leave it
on the doorstep if you want?


00:40:38.708 --> 00:40:40.276
No, no, no.
I'm coming. I'm coming.


00:40:40.308 --> 00:40:42.165
I was just in
the middle of something.


00:40:42.196 --> 00:40:43.316
One second.


00:40:43.827 --> 00:40:46.293
I'm at the window.
Where are you?


00:40:46.323 --> 00:40:48.372
<i>Um, let me
just check on that.</i>


00:40:48.404 --> 00:40:50.165
Sorry, mate. Wrong number.


00:41:00.723 --> 00:41:04.371
I wouldn't use that lav...
uh, bathroom for a bit.


00:41:05.204 --> 00:41:07.604
I'm sorry. You're going to have
to wait here for a moment.


00:41:07.636 --> 00:41:09.141
Brittles?


00:41:09.171 --> 00:41:10.612
Can you come up here, please?


00:41:18.933 --> 00:41:20.501
What is this?


00:41:24.468 --> 00:41:26.228
Search her bag.


00:41:26.772 --> 00:41:27.797
Hey!


00:41:28.467 --> 00:41:29.683
Excuse me!


00:41:34.484 --> 00:41:36.244
If that's the way
you treat all your interns,


00:41:36.275 --> 00:41:37.524
you can take
your work experience


00:41:37.555 --> 00:41:38.965
and shove it up your arse!


00:42:00.467 --> 00:42:02.100
Okay.


00:42:25.780 --> 00:42:28.852
<i>Our Dr. Losberne is gonna
get a surprise in the morning.</i>


00:42:28.883 --> 00:42:31.027
Until then,
you can take the night off.


00:42:31.060 --> 00:42:33.428
- Go out, have some fun.
- Yes!


00:42:33.460 --> 00:42:35.475
Yeah, but wait a minute.
Not too much fun


00:42:35.508 --> 00:42:37.876
because you're back
on duty at 7:00 a.m.


00:42:37.908 --> 00:42:38.963
7:00?


00:42:38.995 --> 00:42:40.819
We've all gotta be ready


00:42:40.852 --> 00:42:42.613
to move when
the phone goes.


00:42:42.643 --> 00:42:44.628
And I'll stay tuned to Losberne.


00:42:44.659 --> 00:42:47.828
Well, you know he might be
into some heavy phone sex,


00:42:47.860 --> 00:42:50.420
which means you might be in
for a steamy night, old boy.


00:42:50.451 --> 00:42:52.308
So there's this party.


00:42:52.340 --> 00:42:54.068
- What you saying?
- Red, you coming?


00:42:54.100 --> 00:42:55.540
She got plans.


00:42:59.700 --> 00:43:01.268
You did good.


00:43:14.131 --> 00:43:15.828
Mate, let's go.
Come on.


00:43:16.436 --> 00:43:17.781
Awkward.


00:43:32.340 --> 00:43:35.476
Come on, mate. Don't be such
a Debbie Downer.


00:43:35.507 --> 00:43:38.068
You know, there are
other birds in London.


00:43:38.548 --> 00:43:40.372
Come on.
Have a drink with us.


00:43:40.403 --> 00:43:42.740
No, I'm all right, mate.
Honestly.


00:43:42.771 --> 00:43:44.723
Come on.
You know you want to.


00:43:44.755 --> 00:43:46.004
Seriously, Batesy.


00:43:46.484 --> 00:43:47.861
I'm all right here.


00:43:48.723 --> 00:43:50.259
All right. Fine.


00:43:58.964 --> 00:44:00.533
- Hey.
- I said...


00:44:01.524 --> 00:44:03.828
Oi. You mug.


00:44:05.140 --> 00:44:06.612
She belongs to Sikes.


00:44:06.643 --> 00:44:08.500
You think
I don't know that?


00:44:08.531 --> 00:44:09.685
I don't belong to anyone.


00:44:17.491 --> 00:44:18.517
We'll see.


00:44:46.451 --> 00:44:48.884
Oi, Batesy!
Batesy, look out!


00:44:59.923 --> 00:45:01.972
I love coming here.


00:45:02.003 --> 00:45:03.892
You almost forget
you're in the city.


00:45:04.404 --> 00:45:06.484
How do you know
about this place?


00:45:06.515 --> 00:45:09.396
Uh, Sikes brought me
here once.


00:45:11.091 --> 00:45:12.500
Why'd you bring me
here then?


00:45:13.491 --> 00:45:16.596
Because I wanted to.
Is that okay?


00:45:17.779 --> 00:45:19.060
Hmm?


00:45:25.588 --> 00:45:27.348
Red!


00:45:38.836 --> 00:45:40.787
Seriously, why did
you bring me here?


00:45:40.819 --> 00:45:42.676
Why wouldn't
I bring you here?


00:45:42.707 --> 00:45:44.947
I don't think your girlfriend
would be too happy if she knew.


00:45:44.979 --> 00:45:46.932
Mmm, never said
she was my girlfriend.


00:45:48.435 --> 00:45:49.716
Why didn't you tell me?


00:45:50.452 --> 00:45:51.732
Tell you what?


00:45:52.852 --> 00:45:54.260
That you're only into...


00:45:54.291 --> 00:45:57.172
Girls?
Never said that either.


00:45:59.923 --> 00:46:01.267
I'm so confused.


00:46:15.347 --> 00:46:17.108
Oi! What the hell
are you doing?


00:46:28.756 --> 00:46:31.028
Hey. Don't tell anyone
about this, yeah?


00:46:31.764 --> 00:46:34.484
Red, if this is about Sikes,
you don't need to be scared.


00:46:34.516 --> 00:46:36.660
It's not me
I'm scared for.


00:46:54.004 --> 00:46:56.084
Got you!


00:46:56.115 --> 00:46:58.676
You think you're clever, don't you?
Call the police, love.


00:46:58.707 --> 00:47:01.044
- I will 'cause you're assaulting him!
- Assaulting him?


00:47:01.075 --> 00:47:03.859
- Yeah!
- This little bellend has been vandalizing property


00:47:03.892 --> 00:47:07.252
of the council with his
shitty little paintings.


00:47:07.283 --> 00:47:09.012
You wanna go as well, eh?


00:47:09.043 --> 00:47:10.323
Come on!


00:47:10.354 --> 00:47:12.467
Here they are.
Get down there, you! Go on.


00:47:12.500 --> 00:47:15.348
She's with the bellend there.
Arrest them.


00:47:15.379 --> 00:47:17.203
- Stay with them. It'll be okay.
- Come on, Son.


00:47:17.652 --> 00:47:18.900
I'll get Fagin.
Go on.


00:47:18.932 --> 00:47:20.628
Thank you.
All right.


00:47:28.564 --> 00:47:30.260
Personally I think
it's an improvement.


00:47:32.051 --> 00:47:33.205
So let me go.


00:47:33.971 --> 00:47:36.947
Unfortunately,
Metropolis Parking Solutions...


00:47:36.978 --> 00:47:39.091
That's the company
whose property you vandalized,


00:47:39.124 --> 00:47:41.909
they don't quite share
the same views.


00:47:47.156 --> 00:47:48.788
Little Ollie Twister.


00:47:54.706 --> 00:47:57.236
Look, to be honest, Oliver,
a little bit of graffiti


00:47:57.268 --> 00:47:59.540
is not really
what concerns me.


00:47:59.955 --> 00:48:01.971
You kind of running
into Warden Bumble,


00:48:02.004 --> 00:48:03.796
well that's just kind
of fortuitous for me.


00:48:03.828 --> 00:48:05.204
It's like
a happy accident.


00:48:05.939 --> 00:48:08.180
What I really wanna talk
to you about is...


00:48:11.795 --> 00:48:13.364
this man.


00:48:14.739 --> 00:48:15.764
Fagin.


00:48:16.594 --> 00:48:18.547
An alias, obviously.


00:48:18.579 --> 00:48:21.107
A once prestigious
art dealer.


00:48:21.139 --> 00:48:22.868
Then out of the blue...


00:48:22.899 --> 00:48:24.532
...vanishes.
Disappears.


00:48:25.203 --> 00:48:27.891
And since then, it seems
like he's been putting


00:48:27.924 --> 00:48:30.613
his knowledge of art
to more practical usage.


00:48:31.124 --> 00:48:33.845
Apparently he's running
quite the operation.


00:48:36.116 --> 00:48:37.429
Yeah.


00:48:38.515 --> 00:48:40.179
And what about
this lovely lady?


00:48:40.211 --> 00:48:41.716
Known associate of Fagin.


00:48:41.746 --> 00:48:43.092
Sikes.


00:48:44.563 --> 00:48:46.292
How am I supposed
to know these two?


00:48:48.114 --> 00:48:49.747
How am I supposed to...


00:48:51.347 --> 00:48:53.812
Nancy Lee, alias Red.


00:48:53.843 --> 00:48:56.755
Known associate of
both Sikes and Fagin's.


00:49:00.051 --> 00:49:01.747
It's a pretty girl,
Oliver.


00:49:07.731 --> 00:49:09.331
I can get you out of this,
you know.


00:49:10.099 --> 00:49:12.851
- Get me out of what?
- Ah, see, now that,


00:49:12.882 --> 00:49:15.187
that's exactly what I'm
hoping you're gonna tell me.


00:49:15.220 --> 00:49:16.852
Because your little friends,
your new pals,


00:49:16.884 --> 00:49:19.573
they're not all
that they seem.


00:49:20.052 --> 00:49:22.452
And to be perfectly honest,
friends of Fagin and Sikes


00:49:22.483 --> 00:49:24.372
have a nasty habit
of ending up, well...


00:49:27.859 --> 00:49:29.428
like that.


00:49:29.458 --> 00:49:31.731
Tom Chitling.
He died last month.


00:49:31.764 --> 00:49:34.132
Take a good look, Oliver.


00:49:34.163 --> 00:49:35.412
I don't even know this Sikes.


00:49:36.467 --> 00:49:38.132
Are you sure?


00:49:39.284 --> 00:49:40.789
I'm sure.


00:49:42.803 --> 00:49:43.829
Okay.


00:49:44.435 --> 00:49:46.515
Well,
you're free to go.


00:49:47.538 --> 00:49:50.803
Just be careful who you trust because
people only see what they wanna see.


00:49:53.267 --> 00:49:54.451
Off you go, then.


00:50:03.411 --> 00:50:04.756
You're late.


00:50:06.099 --> 00:50:07.603
Where's Twist?


00:50:08.691 --> 00:50:09.940
He was with you,
right, Dodge?


00:50:14.996 --> 00:50:17.396
Just wanted to get a run-in.
I lost track of time.


00:50:18.354 --> 00:50:19.668
I don't know
where Twist is.


00:50:19.699 --> 00:50:21.619
I gave them all the night off.


00:50:21.650 --> 00:50:24.371
Those paintings are going
nowhere till the morning.


00:50:24.404 --> 00:50:26.099
It is morning.
Where is he?


00:50:39.764 --> 00:50:41.556
- Who is this?
- <i>Think of me</i>


00:50:41.587 --> 00:50:43.603
<i>as the friendly uncle
you never had.</i>


00:50:43.635 --> 00:50:45.939
<i>I just wanted to make sure
you've got my number.</i>


00:50:46.580 --> 00:50:49.140
<i>In case you remember anything
about our Ms. Sikes.</i>


00:50:49.172 --> 00:50:50.421
I won't.


00:50:51.156 --> 00:50:53.300
You got some explaining
to do, boy.


00:50:55.155 --> 00:50:57.939
- Where you been, then?
- I went to a pub with Dodge and Batesy.


00:50:57.970 --> 00:51:00.403
They got back hours ago.
What happened to you?


00:51:01.395 --> 00:51:04.563
- I got arrested.
- Been having little words, have we?


00:51:04.595 --> 00:51:05.844
No, it wasn't
like that.


00:51:05.876 --> 00:51:07.508
It was this traffic warden.


00:51:07.539 --> 00:51:09.172
I wrote on his van
and he wasn't happy about it.


00:51:09.202 --> 00:51:10.996
You wrote
on his van last night?


00:51:11.027 --> 00:51:12.563
No, last week.


00:51:12.596 --> 00:51:14.259
I bumped into him
this morning...


00:51:14.291 --> 00:51:15.892
How come
the cops let you go?


00:51:16.691 --> 00:51:18.611
Did you give them
something they wanted?


00:51:18.643 --> 00:51:20.500
No, nothing.
I gave them nothing.


00:51:20.532 --> 00:51:21.908
If he grassed,
why would he come back here?


00:51:21.939 --> 00:51:23.092
Was I talking to you?


00:51:23.124 --> 00:51:24.980
- I'm just saying, I...
- Don't!


00:51:25.011 --> 00:51:27.283
- We need him.
- <i>Hello, Artnet.</i>


00:51:27.315 --> 00:51:29.395
- <i>Hello, it's Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>
- Shh!


00:51:29.428 --> 00:51:31.443
<i>My vault is flooded, so I need
to move a painting to Dotheboy's.</i>


00:51:31.474 --> 00:51:33.171
He's on the phone
with the couriers.


00:51:33.202 --> 00:51:34.548
They're arranging a pickup.


00:51:34.579 --> 00:51:36.019
<i>One second.</i>


00:51:37.331 --> 00:51:38.995
Round three.


00:51:40.178 --> 00:51:41.907
The painting is gonna be
on the move.


00:51:41.938 --> 00:51:43.667
This is it.


00:51:43.698 --> 00:51:45.875
You better pray this time
it goes like clockwork.


00:51:48.532 --> 00:51:50.900
Remember,
I'm watching.


00:51:59.604 --> 00:52:01.748
I'm claustrophobic,
okay.


00:52:01.779 --> 00:52:04.212
Nobody told me that
it was gonna be that small.


00:52:04.627 --> 00:52:07.188
- Quit making a fuss and get in.
- I'm not making a fuss.


00:52:07.220 --> 00:52:09.938
I'm claustrophobic.
It's an actual condition.


00:52:09.971 --> 00:52:12.467
If Batesy gets in there
and passes out,


00:52:12.499 --> 00:52:14.356
the whole plan's screwed.
What are we gonna do?


00:52:14.387 --> 00:52:16.372
Exactly. And there is
every chance


00:52:16.403 --> 00:52:18.452
that if I get in there
I will pass out.


00:52:18.483 --> 00:52:20.276
Batesy,
don't be such a baby.


00:52:20.307 --> 00:52:22.323
What are you gonna do?
Force him down?


00:52:22.355 --> 00:52:24.435
You say you're gonna do
something then don't do it.


00:52:24.466 --> 00:52:27.764
Are we gonna do this,
or you gonna stand there arguing all day?


00:52:27.795 --> 00:52:28.884
Well, he's in now.


00:52:30.034 --> 00:52:33.172
All right. Anybody tries
to moves the crate,


00:52:33.204 --> 00:52:35.700
you set off the smoke bomb
in their face.


00:52:36.531 --> 00:52:37.715
Piece of cake.


00:52:38.386 --> 00:52:39.827
All right. That's it.


00:52:42.131 --> 00:52:43.123
Let's do it then.


00:52:46.418 --> 00:52:47.508
Really?


00:52:59.155 --> 00:53:01.363
Delivery to our gallery
in W1, yeah?


00:53:01.395 --> 00:53:02.675
Yeah, copy that, darling.


00:53:02.708 --> 00:53:04.148
We just got
a few drop-offs first.


00:53:04.180 --> 00:53:05.332
Cheers, lads.


00:53:29.235 --> 00:53:31.763
I thought we were only sharing travel
with the National Gallery piece.


00:53:31.795 --> 00:53:33.331
Uh, let me see.


00:53:33.362 --> 00:53:34.996
Originally yours
was dropped off first


00:53:35.027 --> 00:53:36.372
and then on
to the National Gallery.


00:53:36.403 --> 00:53:38.068
It's just an extra
pickup, mate.


00:53:38.098 --> 00:53:39.444
It won't affect
your drop-off time.


00:53:39.474 --> 00:53:41.842
They're close together,
you see.


00:53:41.874 --> 00:53:45.715
- Chiswell Fine Arts.
- I've never heard of it.


00:53:52.307 --> 00:53:54.707
You ever heard of
a Chiswell Fine Arts, Rosie?


00:53:54.739 --> 00:53:56.275
Somewhere near here?


00:53:56.690 --> 00:53:58.899
I thought you knew all
the galleries in London.


00:54:01.779 --> 00:54:03.763
I'll google it.


00:54:09.682 --> 00:54:12.084
Can't find a Chiswell.


00:54:14.803 --> 00:54:16.563
Get me Artnet
on the phone now!


00:54:37.811 --> 00:54:39.476
What's all this?


00:54:46.098 --> 00:54:47.379
You all right?
What's occurring?


00:54:47.410 --> 00:54:49.268
- Can we get through?
- How you doing?


00:54:49.298 --> 00:54:50.708
- Yeah, fine.
- Where you from?


00:54:50.739 --> 00:54:52.275
- I'm from Fullham.
- Fullham?


00:54:52.306 --> 00:54:55.091
I've got cousins in Fullham.
You know Phil?


00:54:55.123 --> 00:54:57.043
- No.
- You must know my second cousin.


00:54:57.075 --> 00:54:58.835
- What's her name? Oh, Tracey.
- No.


00:54:58.867 --> 00:55:00.659
- Can we get through?
- Can you get through?


00:55:00.691 --> 00:55:02.803
I don't know...


00:55:02.835 --> 00:55:05.396
<i>7-4, receiving. 7-4, receiving.</i>


00:55:05.426 --> 00:55:07.252
Is there aliens?
I mean...


00:55:07.282 --> 00:55:08.691
7-4. Go ahead.


00:55:08.723 --> 00:55:10.867
<i>Just had a call from
the Losberne Gallery.</i>


00:55:10.900 --> 00:55:13.139
<i>They seem to think
they're being robbed.</i>


00:55:13.171 --> 00:55:16.115
Is it real?
Is life even real?


00:55:16.147 --> 00:55:17.587
Everything all right,
lads?


00:55:18.675 --> 00:55:20.211
Floor it!


00:55:34.418 --> 00:55:36.019
No!


00:55:37.524 --> 00:55:39.667
Sikes, no.
No, Sikes!


00:55:40.211 --> 00:55:41.716
Please, Sikes.


00:55:44.691 --> 00:55:45.811
Run!


00:55:46.772 --> 00:55:49.619
- Where is it? Give it to me.
- I didn't get it. I'm sorry.


00:55:49.651 --> 00:55:52.691
We need a distraction.
Move. Move!


00:55:57.394 --> 00:55:59.442
When I said "don't,"
that means don't go this way.


00:55:59.475 --> 00:56:01.811
- <i>...female in a red leather jacket.</i>
- Hey!


00:56:01.842 --> 00:56:03.826
Female suspect heading west
down Pass Road.


00:56:03.859 --> 00:56:06.227
<i>Officers are in pursuit.
Officers are in pursuit.</i>


00:56:19.060 --> 00:56:20.628
I'm asking you
very nicely to stop.


00:56:24.275 --> 00:56:25.524
There it is.


00:56:49.938 --> 00:56:51.860
I really need
to start going to the gym.


00:56:52.755 --> 00:56:53.875
This is...


00:57:04.499 --> 00:57:05.748
Uh...


00:57:07.442 --> 00:57:09.170
<i>Bedwin, give me an update.</i>


00:57:09.202 --> 00:57:11.411
Brownlow, we got some good news
and some bad news.


00:57:11.443 --> 00:57:13.906
- <i>Fill me in then.</i>
- Yeah, well, the bad news is I haven't got her.


00:57:14.034 --> 00:57:17.075
- <i>What's the good news?</i>
- There is no good news, really, if I'm honest.


00:57:17.107 --> 00:57:18.803
<i>Get yourself back here now.</i>


00:57:25.747 --> 00:57:27.283
Oi! Get in.


00:57:28.084 --> 00:57:30.323
- I need to work on my cardio.
- How come Twist was


00:57:30.355 --> 00:57:32.084
in the back of that van?
Should have been you.


00:57:32.979 --> 00:57:36.243
Well, I'm claustrophobic,
so we just switched places.


00:57:38.740 --> 00:57:40.084
You shouldn't have.


00:57:47.027 --> 00:57:48.564
Batesy!


00:58:24.146 --> 00:58:25.874
He should have been
back by now.


00:58:25.906 --> 00:58:27.859
Quiet. I'm trying to think.


00:58:28.308 --> 00:58:30.515
That was our one shot.


00:58:31.954 --> 00:58:33.906
It was bad luck
is all.


00:58:34.355 --> 00:58:35.859
Bad luck? There's no such thing.


00:58:35.891 --> 00:58:38.547
It was a simple plan
until that bloody Twist


00:58:38.579 --> 00:58:40.754
decided to go in the van.


00:58:46.994 --> 00:58:48.852
Mate, have you seen...


00:58:51.123 --> 00:58:52.691
What happened
to Tom Chitling?


00:58:52.723 --> 00:58:53.811
He fell.


00:58:55.570 --> 00:58:59.410
- Did you see it?
- Someone has been misinforming you, Oliver.


00:58:59.443 --> 00:59:03.859
- Don't avoid the question!
- I just don't think it's you asking the questions.


00:59:03.891 --> 00:59:05.812
Who have you been talking to?


00:59:08.467 --> 00:59:09.972
Sikes.


00:59:10.578 --> 00:59:12.787
Why don't you ask her?


00:59:13.907 --> 00:59:15.699
- Sikes!
- He's a rat!


00:59:16.179 --> 00:59:18.227
Van suddenly peels off.
They knew what was going down.


00:59:18.259 --> 00:59:19.668
- I didn't tell them anything!
- Lies!


00:59:21.715 --> 00:59:23.059
What's this, eh?


00:59:25.683 --> 00:59:27.507
Thing I need to know, Twist,


00:59:27.539 --> 00:59:29.267
is how you hold up
under a beating.


00:59:29.811 --> 00:59:31.154
I bet you fall
to pieces, eh?


00:59:31.187 --> 00:59:32.403
Fagin, make her stop.


00:59:40.946 --> 00:59:42.674
Question is,
do you want some more?


00:59:45.459 --> 00:59:46.580
Hold him.


00:59:47.923 --> 00:59:50.002
Sikes, don't make it
permanent.


00:59:50.034 --> 00:59:51.763
Right, Bullseye,
on my command.


00:59:53.202 --> 00:59:55.154
You're making a mistake.


00:59:55.634 --> 00:59:57.043
A mistake?


00:59:57.906 --> 00:59:59.828
He got in trouble
with the traffic warden.


00:59:59.859 --> 01:00:01.716
And how would
you know that, Red?


01:00:02.354 --> 01:00:03.732
'Cause I was there.


01:00:04.850 --> 01:00:05.971
What?


01:00:08.211 --> 01:00:10.067
We were on our way home
and the traffic warden


01:00:10.099 --> 01:00:11.923
came out of nowhere
and tackled him to the ground.


01:00:11.955 --> 01:00:13.907
- Just like he said.
- On your way home from where?


01:00:16.498 --> 01:00:17.587
We...


01:00:18.803 --> 01:00:20.660
We went for a swim together.


01:00:33.651 --> 01:00:35.475
If he moves, shoot him.


01:00:35.507 --> 01:00:37.555
Come with me.


01:00:37.586 --> 01:00:38.803
Bullseye, stay.


01:00:51.475 --> 01:00:53.171
This ain't like Batesy.


01:00:53.202 --> 01:00:55.186
He gets withdrawal symptoms
if he ain't plugged in.


01:00:55.219 --> 01:00:57.523
- Batesy's dead.
- What?


01:00:57.554 --> 01:00:58.835
Just like she killed Tom.


01:00:59.410 --> 01:01:01.490
- But Sikes said...
- Tom was murdered!


01:01:02.226 --> 01:01:04.370
He didn't go off
that roof by accident.


01:01:05.651 --> 01:01:07.059
How would you know that?


01:01:08.211 --> 01:01:09.460
I got a text
off that phone.


01:01:11.026 --> 01:01:12.562
Some cop gave it to me
to see if I'd turn.


01:01:12.595 --> 01:01:14.323
And did you turn?


01:01:14.355 --> 01:01:17.300
Or were you never
with this family to begin with?


01:01:17.810 --> 01:01:19.475
You call this a family?


01:01:20.179 --> 01:01:21.746
When that psycho is
out there with Red


01:01:21.779 --> 01:01:23.379
and you're pointing
a gun at me!


01:01:24.531 --> 01:01:25.747
I don't believe you.


01:01:25.778 --> 01:01:27.314
I'm gonna go find Batesy myself.


01:01:27.347 --> 01:01:28.852
You're gonna be looking
six feet under.


01:01:29.299 --> 01:01:32.083
He's right. I pushed Tom.


01:01:32.114 --> 01:01:33.970
- You lying piece...
- Please.


01:01:34.002 --> 01:01:35.795
Give me an excuse to kill you.


01:01:36.211 --> 01:01:37.427
You can't kill all of us.


01:01:38.194 --> 01:01:39.379
Let's see, shall we?


01:01:39.955 --> 01:01:42.163
Six bullets, three kids.
You do the math.


01:01:42.195 --> 01:01:44.531
We're hitting Dotheboy's.
We're getting that painting.


01:01:44.563 --> 01:01:46.419
Dotheboy's?
I think the whole plan


01:01:46.450 --> 01:01:48.946
was to get the painting
before it went there.


01:01:48.978 --> 01:01:51.187
That place
is impenetrable.


01:01:51.219 --> 01:01:52.819
You scared, old man?


01:01:53.330 --> 01:01:55.731
I'll have a plan
in four hours.


01:01:56.242 --> 01:01:59.283
Try not to kill any more
of them in the meantime.


01:02:01.938 --> 01:02:03.251
I can't promise anything.


01:02:11.698 --> 01:02:13.810
<i>Look, mate,
I believe ya.</i>


01:02:14.483 --> 01:02:16.819
<i>What Sikes did to Tom,
that's messed up.</i>


01:02:17.394 --> 01:02:19.699
But if we don't do this,
we'll lose Red too.


01:02:21.203 --> 01:02:22.963
Sikes is a loose cannon.


01:02:22.994 --> 01:02:25.043
Let's just suck it up
and get on with it, yeah?


01:02:26.738 --> 01:02:28.083
Let's do this.


01:02:34.770 --> 01:02:35.858
<i>Is he on time?</i>


01:02:35.890 --> 01:02:38.580
Like clockwork. We're on.


01:02:51.027 --> 01:02:52.691
Can I get two sugars
with that, as well?


01:02:53.426 --> 01:02:55.154
All right there, mates?
Sorry to interrupt.


01:02:55.186 --> 01:02:57.010
Can I get a Bakewell tart,
please?


01:02:57.042 --> 01:02:58.547
Sure.


01:02:59.059 --> 01:03:00.883
- It's chippy, innit?
- Yeah, I know. It's freezing.


01:03:00.915 --> 01:03:02.643
There you go. 1.50.


01:03:03.092 --> 01:03:04.434
There you go.
Keep the change.


01:03:05.682 --> 01:03:06.772
Thanks.


01:03:09.011 --> 01:03:10.322
Have a good day,
lads.


01:03:10.354 --> 01:03:11.539
See ya.


01:03:25.874 --> 01:03:29.330
<i>The painting will be under
lock and key before the auction.</i>


01:03:29.746 --> 01:03:32.691
<i>So our only chance is
during the main event.</i>


01:03:32.722 --> 01:03:35.410
<i>We'll go in at the front
and at the right moment</i>


01:03:35.443 --> 01:03:38.323
<i>execute the plan,
sending the painting your way.</i>


01:03:38.354 --> 01:03:40.371
Let's play happy families, eh?
Big smiles.


01:03:58.259 --> 01:03:59.923
Thank you.


01:03:59.954 --> 01:04:01.874
Whoa, whoa.


01:04:01.906 --> 01:04:03.923
It's the chair. Really?


01:04:04.435 --> 01:04:05.619
Jesus.


01:04:22.226 --> 01:04:24.242
There you go.


01:04:24.274 --> 01:04:26.899
<i>Dodge, once you're
inside, let Twist in.</i>


01:04:26.931 --> 01:04:29.010
<i>Then, when all hell
has broken loose,</i>


01:04:29.042 --> 01:04:30.162
<i>you know what to do.</i>


01:04:35.603 --> 01:04:36.851
Gang's all here.


01:04:45.330 --> 01:04:47.123
Don't do anything stupid.


01:04:56.083 --> 01:04:58.930
I'm glad you're finally taking
this threat seriously, Officer.


01:05:00.594 --> 01:05:02.196
Detective Inspector.


01:05:08.562 --> 01:05:09.972
How many men
have you deployed?


01:05:11.091 --> 01:05:12.435
There's 12
inside the building.


01:05:13.266 --> 01:05:14.963
Another 20 outside.


01:05:18.610 --> 01:05:20.115
Nobody is getting
this painting, Losberne.


01:05:20.146 --> 01:05:21.779
Doctor Losberne.


01:05:31.762 --> 01:05:33.394
Better you than me,
mate.


01:05:49.618 --> 01:05:51.187
<i>Lot 146.</i>


01:05:51.923 --> 01:05:53.714
William Hogarth's painting


01:05:53.746 --> 01:05:56.435
<i>A Harlot's Progress,
The Arrest.</i>


01:05:56.466 --> 01:05:59.346
Oil on canvas. 1731.


01:05:59.378 --> 01:06:01.458
Has resurfaced
after many years,


01:06:01.490 --> 01:06:04.242
as the only surviving <i>Harlot's
Progress</i> from the fire...


01:06:04.274 --> 01:06:05.779
Now.


01:06:06.355 --> 01:06:09.939
We start the reserve
price of three million pounds.


01:06:09.969 --> 01:06:11.442
Yes, madam.


01:06:12.818 --> 01:06:15.570
And you, sir? At the back there, sir? Yes.


01:06:15.603 --> 01:06:17.203
Three million two.


01:06:17.235 --> 01:06:18.771
I have three million,
200 thousand pounds.


01:06:21.041 --> 01:06:22.547
He's got a gun!


01:06:24.499 --> 01:06:26.419
- Stay calm.
- It was a trap.


01:06:26.449 --> 01:06:29.138
- They're after my painting!
- Get it back in the vault!


01:06:29.170 --> 01:06:30.835
It'll be safe.
It's the safest place.


01:06:36.115 --> 01:06:38.514
- Over there, look.
- Through that door.


01:06:43.282 --> 01:06:46.003
There's a robbery in progress.
Stay with the painting.


01:06:46.035 --> 01:06:47.891
Get it to the vault.
Let's go! Let's move.


01:06:51.122 --> 01:06:53.042
Wait, wait, wait.


01:06:53.074 --> 01:06:54.739
I'm coming with you.


01:06:54.770 --> 01:06:56.083
No one goes
down there but us.


01:06:56.114 --> 01:06:57.875
There's a robbery in progress.


01:06:57.907 --> 01:07:00.786
- Yeah, we have our procedures.
- And I have my orders.


01:07:00.819 --> 01:07:03.571
And that painting ain't going
anywhere without me.


01:07:03.603 --> 01:07:05.555
What... What's going on?


01:07:05.586 --> 01:07:08.371
- Who are you?
- Officer Dawkins, Sergeant.


01:07:08.402 --> 01:07:10.162
- Dawkins? Good.
- Yeah.


01:07:51.923 --> 01:07:54.707
Okay. You guys go that way.
You guys come with me. Let's go.


01:08:00.946 --> 01:08:02.130
You.


01:08:02.802 --> 01:08:05.171
Yes, it's me.


01:08:06.801 --> 01:08:08.754
Ah, that felt good.


01:08:24.370 --> 01:08:26.419
Good. This is good.
This is very good.


01:08:27.442 --> 01:08:28.948
Whoa, whoa, whoa.


01:08:32.210 --> 01:08:33.396
Show me the painting.


01:08:34.993 --> 01:08:35.986
Ah...


01:08:37.842 --> 01:08:39.698
I'll be honest,
not his best work.


01:08:43.538 --> 01:08:44.947
Move!


01:08:44.978 --> 01:08:45.971
Okay.


01:08:50.066 --> 01:08:51.890
Oh, you silly sausage.


01:08:51.922 --> 01:08:53.203
You're going nowhere, Son.


01:08:55.057 --> 01:08:56.563
Shit!


01:08:58.515 --> 01:09:00.530
Brownlow,
you're wrong about Twist.


01:09:00.562 --> 01:09:02.003
He's in the lift shaft.


01:09:02.034 --> 01:09:03.762
Yeah, the dirty swine.


01:09:05.266 --> 01:09:06.740
Well, move then.


01:09:10.418 --> 01:09:12.434
I'm coming for you, Twist.


01:09:12.465 --> 01:09:15.379
- No, no, no!
- If you think a lift is gonna stop me...


01:09:16.275 --> 01:09:19.091
- Oh, you got nowhere to hide, boy.
- Dodge!


01:09:19.123 --> 01:09:20.179
- You muppet.
- Dodge?


01:09:20.210 --> 01:09:22.034
You...


01:09:22.065 --> 01:09:23.122
Hurry up.


01:09:23.154 --> 01:09:24.338
- Dodge.
- Come on.


01:09:24.370 --> 01:09:25.618
Help me!


01:09:25.651 --> 01:09:27.539
- Hurry up.
- Help!


01:09:27.570 --> 01:09:29.555
- Come on.
- I'm coming!


01:09:29.587 --> 01:09:31.219
Get these bloody doors open!


01:09:40.658 --> 01:09:41.907
Hurry up, Dodge!


01:09:55.441 --> 01:09:56.946
Oi!


01:10:03.345 --> 01:10:04.881
Wait a minute.


01:10:04.913 --> 01:10:06.866
Give me a break.
You're not thinking we...


01:10:06.898 --> 01:10:09.075
- Oi! Stop!
- Come on!


01:10:11.698 --> 01:10:14.259
- Ready? Belt.
- Twist, what are you doing? This is madness.


01:10:14.289 --> 01:10:15.858
Three, two, one...


01:10:19.154 --> 01:10:20.338
Hang on!


01:10:21.138 --> 01:10:22.643
Wait, wait...


01:10:22.674 --> 01:10:23.858
Let go!


01:10:29.810 --> 01:10:31.602
Okay.


01:10:31.634 --> 01:10:32.882
Congratulations.


01:10:33.907 --> 01:10:35.027
All the best.


01:10:38.738 --> 01:10:40.627
Brownlow, you need
to get down here right now.


01:10:46.065 --> 01:10:47.314
Shit!


01:10:47.346 --> 01:10:50.706
Shit, shit!


01:10:50.738 --> 01:10:52.818
- Flippin' hell.
- Let's go up here.


01:10:54.737 --> 01:10:56.499
I think we've lost them.


01:10:56.529 --> 01:10:58.579
They wouldn't have got far,
Losberne.


01:10:58.610 --> 01:10:59.954
Well,
you better be right.


01:11:00.594 --> 01:11:02.386
- Come on. Let's go.
- Hey! Hey!


01:11:02.417 --> 01:11:03.923
Don't even think about it!
Do not move.


01:11:03.953 --> 01:11:06.225
Hello?


01:11:06.257 --> 01:11:08.306
- <i>Your delivery's here.</i>
- I didn't order anything.


01:11:09.043 --> 01:11:11.443
- Hey, don't!
- Dodge, let's go!


01:11:12.434 --> 01:11:13.906
Hey!


01:11:13.938 --> 01:11:15.955
Get after them!
Don't leave, hey!


01:11:15.985 --> 01:11:18.035
- Come back here! Come...
- Wait!


01:11:18.066 --> 01:11:21.074
Get them... Hey, stop!


01:11:21.105 --> 01:11:23.666
Stop! Make him stop!


01:11:41.107 --> 01:11:43.891
There's only one person
who could do this.


01:11:49.970 --> 01:11:51.506
<i>Batesy.</i>


01:11:51.537 --> 01:11:52.850
Enjoy your munch, did ya?


01:11:52.882 --> 01:11:55.378
You magnificent bastard.


01:11:55.411 --> 01:11:59.282
You had us worried sick, mate.
Where are ya?


01:11:59.313 --> 01:12:02.130
You know Sikes has gone
full-blown psycho, don't you?


01:12:02.162 --> 01:12:03.825
- <i>She tried to kill me.</i>
- What?


01:12:03.858 --> 01:12:05.331
We're on our way
to see her now.


01:12:05.362 --> 01:12:07.186
<i>No, don't! It ain't safe.</i>


01:12:07.218 --> 01:12:09.715
What do you mean?
We got no choice.


01:12:09.746 --> 01:12:11.891
<i>Red's with her.
We're all heading to Fagin's.</i>


01:12:13.043 --> 01:12:14.675
All right, well,
I'll meet you there.


01:12:14.707 --> 01:12:16.211
- <i>Just look after yourself.</i>
- Okay.


01:12:17.393 --> 01:12:19.442
That was Batesy. He's...


01:12:22.034 --> 01:12:23.218
Twist?


01:12:27.698 --> 01:12:28.914
Twist?


01:12:32.657 --> 01:12:34.483
You're late.
Where is he?


01:12:35.057 --> 01:12:36.786
I don't know.
We got split up.


01:12:36.817 --> 01:12:38.385
- Who's got it?
- He has.


01:12:38.418 --> 01:12:39.635
Oi!


01:12:40.562 --> 01:12:42.706
- You miss me?
- Bates.


01:12:43.282 --> 01:12:45.106
You all right?
What happened?


01:12:45.137 --> 01:12:47.251
Thought I dealt with you,
fuck's sake.


01:12:47.281 --> 01:12:49.361
- Where's Twist?
- I'm right here.


01:12:57.202 --> 01:12:59.058
You want the painting?
She's coming with me.


01:13:00.339 --> 01:13:01.779
Do you think she's worth it?


01:13:05.521 --> 01:13:06.514
Try me.


01:13:08.050 --> 01:13:09.651
Do what he says.


01:13:14.258 --> 01:13:16.339
You got more stones than
I gave you credit for.


01:13:18.129 --> 01:13:19.635
Give me that.


01:13:25.489 --> 01:13:27.442
I'll always be
a step ahead of you.


01:13:30.833 --> 01:13:32.690
You think
you can just take my girl?


01:13:34.065 --> 01:13:35.090
It's the painting, Sikes.


01:13:35.537 --> 01:13:37.746
Give me the envelope
and let him go.


01:13:38.834 --> 01:13:39.954
You sure that's it, Fagin?


01:13:44.850 --> 01:13:46.771
- What?
- The painting.


01:13:47.441 --> 01:13:48.818
Are you sure
it's the right one?


01:13:53.522 --> 01:13:55.411
Easy. Easy.


01:13:55.985 --> 01:13:57.650
I'm just reaching for my phone.


01:13:58.225 --> 01:14:00.146
You guys might wanna see this.


01:14:06.098 --> 01:14:07.955
You see,
before I got into graffiti,


01:14:08.722 --> 01:14:10.387
I used to paint.


01:14:10.418 --> 01:14:13.681
You lot mentioning Hogarth
got me inspired.


01:14:13.714 --> 01:14:15.539
It's not bad, eh, Fagin?


01:14:16.305 --> 01:14:17.490
Where is it?


01:14:17.873 --> 01:14:19.571
I walk out of here
with Red.


01:14:20.305 --> 01:14:22.098
I'll call you
and tell you where it is.


01:14:22.129 --> 01:14:23.475
She stays with me.


01:14:24.881 --> 01:14:26.482
We need the painting, Sikes.


01:14:26.513 --> 01:14:28.370
Whose side are you on?


01:14:28.402 --> 01:14:31.507
All this has got to stop.
You're done. We're done.


01:14:31.539 --> 01:14:33.523
All bets are off.


01:14:33.554 --> 01:14:36.626
Get me the envelope
and I'll let you leave.


01:14:50.098 --> 01:14:51.281
Come on.


01:14:52.178 --> 01:14:53.713
You'll let me leave?


01:14:59.954 --> 01:15:01.650
I choose how this ends.


01:15:02.673 --> 01:15:04.307
- Fagin, Fagin.
- Fagin.


01:15:04.818 --> 01:15:05.811
Fagin?


01:15:11.890 --> 01:15:13.266
Come on!


01:15:14.002 --> 01:15:16.146
Quick! Come on, Twist!


01:15:28.657 --> 01:15:30.066
Come on!


01:15:34.578 --> 01:15:36.019
You go first.


01:15:36.050 --> 01:15:37.491
I'm not going without you!


01:15:37.522 --> 01:15:39.763
Listen, jump.
I'll be right behind you.


01:15:40.273 --> 01:15:41.266
Go.


01:15:58.353 --> 01:16:00.145
Twist! Twist.


01:16:00.177 --> 01:16:01.426
Hold on, hold on.


01:16:01.457 --> 01:16:03.027
Come on!


01:16:07.794 --> 01:16:10.098
Twist! Come on.


01:16:10.130 --> 01:16:11.474
Don't let go.


01:16:19.089 --> 01:16:21.074
No! No!


01:16:24.019 --> 01:16:27.155
- Pull him up, Sikes.
- I'm sure he'll be fine. Step back!


01:16:27.185 --> 01:16:29.265
Look at him, not even strong
enough to pull himself up.


01:16:29.298 --> 01:16:31.826
- He's so weak.
- He's not weak!


01:16:31.858 --> 01:16:34.642
- You need to come with me now.
- I don't need you anymore.


01:16:34.673 --> 01:16:36.402
You think Twist is
the one for you?


01:16:36.433 --> 01:16:37.811
He's more than
you will ever be.


01:16:37.841 --> 01:16:39.539
I dragged you from the gutter,
looked after you,


01:16:39.570 --> 01:16:41.330
gave you everything
you needed.


01:16:41.361 --> 01:16:42.610
Sikes!


01:16:59.410 --> 01:17:02.643
What a fine thing
capital punishment is.


01:17:35.378 --> 01:17:36.851
Young man.


01:17:40.081 --> 01:17:42.002
I'm guessing you heard
about the reward?


01:17:46.065 --> 01:17:47.667
Be there in five.


01:17:52.689 --> 01:17:55.089
Do we know what we're meant
to be waiting for?


01:17:55.121 --> 01:17:57.299
We don't have a clue,
Bedwin.


01:17:57.329 --> 01:17:59.315
I'm sure we'll know
when we see it.


01:17:59.346 --> 01:18:01.491
He's not exactly just gonna stroll in.


01:18:01.521 --> 01:18:04.050
- He's literally just strolled in.
- All right, lads?


01:18:04.561 --> 01:18:06.961
- You hungry?
- You got a lot of nerve showing up.


01:18:06.993 --> 01:18:09.106
- Let's just nick him now.
- Calm down, Bedwin.


01:18:09.138 --> 01:18:10.802
You look like you could do
with a bacon sarnie.


01:18:10.834 --> 01:18:12.562
This might be funny to you,
but this is serious.


01:18:12.592 --> 01:18:13.809
I need your full cooperation.


01:18:13.842 --> 01:18:15.859
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Cooperation?


01:18:16.466 --> 01:18:18.035
I've done you guys a favor.


01:18:18.801 --> 01:18:20.434
How's that?


01:18:20.466 --> 01:18:21.554
Where's the painting?


01:18:21.584 --> 01:18:22.867
I don't have it.


01:18:22.898 --> 01:18:24.402
So where is it?


01:18:24.434 --> 01:18:26.161
I'm not the criminal here.
In fact,


01:18:26.194 --> 01:18:27.698
I've done all the work
for you guys.


01:18:27.729 --> 01:18:29.586
Two bacon sarnies.


01:18:29.617 --> 01:18:30.866
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


01:18:30.897 --> 01:18:32.530
Excuse me. I didn't order this.


01:18:32.562 --> 01:18:34.835
Oh, no, it's fine.
It's my treat.


01:18:34.865 --> 01:18:36.977
Well, that's very kind of you,
young man.


01:18:37.010 --> 01:18:40.178
- Yes, very kind.
- But don't think this is getting you out of trouble.


01:18:40.209 --> 01:18:41.522
I need you to understand
one thing.


01:18:41.553 --> 01:18:43.313
You're gonna need
to start cooperating.


01:18:46.609 --> 01:18:48.017
Oh, brilliant.


01:18:58.130 --> 01:19:00.082
Yeah, hello?
Very smart that was.


01:19:00.113 --> 01:19:01.777
<i>A wise cop
once said to me,</i>


01:19:01.808 --> 01:19:03.729
<i>"People only see
what they wanna see."</i>


01:19:03.761 --> 01:19:06.577
<i>You'll be wanting some
brown sauce with those I assume.</i>


01:19:06.608 --> 01:19:09.266
What do you mean... Hello? Hello?


01:19:12.017 --> 01:19:13.329
Brown sauce.


01:19:16.433 --> 01:19:17.713
Nah, it's...


01:19:21.233 --> 01:19:22.769
It's above
the brown sauce, Bedwin.


01:19:22.801 --> 01:19:24.307
It's above
the brown sauce.


01:19:26.353 --> 01:19:27.890
Holy shit.


01:19:42.097 --> 01:19:45.618
<i>The tale of the stolen Hogarth
in an audacious raid</i>


01:19:45.650 --> 01:19:47.602
<i>took a bizarre twist today</i>


01:19:47.632 --> 01:19:50.930
<i>when a tip-off led detectives
to a lockup in East London</i>


01:19:50.962 --> 01:19:54.770
<i>in which a large collection of
stolen artworks has been discovered.</i>


01:19:54.802 --> 01:19:58.931
<i>The lockup belongs to the art
dealer Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>


01:19:59.505 --> 01:20:03.186
<i>Documents were also found
proving that Dr. Crispin Losberne</i>


01:20:03.217 --> 01:20:06.130
<i>is not the legal owner
of the Hogarth.</i>


01:20:06.162 --> 01:20:09.106
<i>It's alleged that
the well-established art dealer</i>


01:20:09.138 --> 01:20:12.659
<i>has been making his fortune
out of selling stolen artwork</i>


01:20:12.690 --> 01:20:15.282
<i>and faking
the ownership documentation.</i>


01:20:15.314 --> 01:20:18.706
<i>A Mr. Isaac Solomon
has been named as an accomplice.</i>


01:20:18.737 --> 01:20:22.259
<i>It's believed that this man
also goes by the name of Fagin.</i>


01:20:22.865 --> 01:20:25.458
<i>Fagin and Sikes really
had raised some good thieves.</i>


01:20:25.489 --> 01:20:28.305
<i>So good they didn't know
when they were the target.</i>


01:20:33.138 --> 01:20:35.666
<i>The envelope revealed
the true owners of the Hogarth</i>


01:20:35.697 --> 01:20:38.898
<i>and the key to the lockup where
Losberne kept the stolen paintings.</i>


01:20:49.233 --> 01:20:52.882
- Holy shit.
- <i>Even Bedwin and Brownlow deserved a break.</i>


01:20:52.912 --> 01:20:55.026
<i>In other arts-related news,</i>


01:20:55.057 --> 01:20:58.545
<i>a mystery painting arrived
with a special delivery</i>


01:20:58.576 --> 01:21:01.713
<i>for a new exhibition at
the National Gallery last week.</i>


01:21:01.745 --> 01:21:05.426
<i>The question everyone's asking
is: How did it get there?</i>


01:21:06.066 --> 01:21:09.169
<i>The painting was added
to the exhibition by mistake</i>


01:21:09.202 --> 01:21:12.338
<i>but critics have gone wild
for this unknown artist</i>


01:21:12.369 --> 01:21:15.090
<i>and have demanded
the piece remains on display.</i>


01:21:20.274 --> 01:21:21.714
There you go, Mum.


01:21:25.617 --> 01:21:29.553
<i>In fact, people can't stop
talking about the mystery artist,</i>


01:21:29.586 --> 01:21:32.306
<i>with many asking
who is Molly Twist</i>


01:21:32.337 --> 01:21:35.378
<i>and when and where
will all of her work appear.</i>


01:21:35.408 --> 01:21:38.769
<i>Dealers are said to be willing
to offer up to 50,000</i>


01:21:38.800 --> 01:21:41.809
<i>to anyone with
an original Twist painting.</i>


01:21:59.312 --> 01:22:00.913
Cheers, Nancy.


01:22:02.929 --> 01:22:05.777
Call me that again, Oliver,
and I will twist something you don't like.


01:22:08.049 --> 01:22:10.098
All right, quit canoodling.


01:22:12.752 --> 01:22:15.858
So, are you gonna stick
with us, kid?


01:22:15.889 --> 01:22:17.682
Come on,
you know you wanna.


01:22:17.714 --> 01:22:20.114
Look, if I'm gonna be
staying around,


01:22:20.145 --> 01:22:22.161
we gotta cut out all
the nonsense and go straight.


01:22:22.192 --> 01:22:25.361
- Whoa, wait.
- He's joking, right? That must be a joke.


01:22:25.393 --> 01:22:28.850
What exactly do you expect
us lot to do for a job, eh?


01:22:29.553 --> 01:22:31.506
You ever thought about
selling paintings?


01:22:32.466 --> 01:22:34.866
A bag full of Molly Twist art
is worth a few quid.


01:22:36.401 --> 01:22:37.394
Hmm?


01:22:38.193 --> 01:22:41.489
<i>Like I said, no singing,
no dancing.</i>


01:22:41.522 --> 01:22:43.602
<i>But maybe I was wrong about
the happy ending.</i>


01:22:44.562 --> 01:22:47.314
<i>I know these people.
I belong with them.</i>


01:25:35.282 --> 01:25:37.907
